==English==
{{was wotd|2008|October|28}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₂ger-}}
From {{der|en|la|gregārius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɹɪˈɡɛə.ɹɪ.əs/|a=UK}}
* {{IPA|en|/ɡɹɪˈɡɛɹ.i.əs/|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-gregarious.ogg|a=US}}
* {{audio|en|en-au-gregarious.ogg|a=AU}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|of a person}} Describing one who enjoys being in [[crowd]]s and [[socializing]].
# {{lb|en|zoology}} Of animals that travel in [[herd]]s or [[pack]]s.
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|chapter=32|page=151|passage=The Fin-Back is not '''gregarious'''. He seems a whale-hater, as some men are man-haters.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1972|author=w:Richard Adams|title=w:Watership Down
|passage=Rabbits are lively at nightfall, and when evening rain drives them underground they still feel '''gregarious'''.}}
# {{lb|en|botany}} Growing in open [[cluster]]s or colonies; not matted together.
# Pertaining to a [[flock]] or [[crowd]].

